abstract: >-
  AlloQuant is a two-module analysis suite that turns AlphaFold3 structural
  ensembles into quantitative readouts of kinase regulation. Module 1 assigns
  canonical kinase landmarks by profile-HMM alignment to the Pfam Pkinase model,
  so one definition applies across the kinome without fixed residue numbering,
  and measures inter-landmark distances and angles from which it makes
  categorical conformational calls. Module 2 discovers metastable states,
  quantifies internal network rigidity as the mean absolute correlation among
  those measurements, and identifies sub-angstrom differential drivers between
  conditions or states. This repository also archives the derived tables
  underlying every number reported in the accompanying paper.
